invariant: INV-13
file: io.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: a tcp-nonblocking ch_read turns an empty recv at a record boundary
  into CH_EIO, so a caller that has no record yet loses the session. A
  caller that received a ticket-only record would have to hold it back
  until a data record arrived (docs/decisions.md entry 46).

--- old
    if (got == 0) {
        return CH_RECORD_AGAIN;
    }
--- new
    if (got == 0) {
        return CH_EIO;
    }
